Full text: LICENSES/MIT.txt

## GPL-2.0-or-later

A small number of files under
`layers/meta-ast2600-secureboot/vbootrom-ast2600/` are ported
near-verbatim from U-Boot (`sha256.c`/`.h`, `sha512.c`/`.h`, `aes.c`/`.h`,
`rsa_mod_exp.c`, `rsa.h`, `pkcs15.h`) and remain under U-Boot's own
GPL-2.0-or-later license, as their own header comments state. The three
`.patch` files under `qemu-patches/` and
`recipes-bsp/u-boot/u-boot-aspeed-sdk/` are diffs against QEMU and
U-Boot (both GPL-2.0-or-later) and are licensed the same way, via a
`.license` sidecar file next to each patch.

Full text: LICENSES/GPL-2.0-or-later.txt

## How to tell which license applies to a given file

Every source, script, and config file carries its own
`SPDX-License-Identifier` tag — as its first line where the file format
allows a comment, or in a `<filename>.license` sidecar file where it
doesn't (JSON, one .conf file with no comment syntax, and the three
`.patch` files, left untouched so they still apply cleanly with
`git am`). This follows the [REUSE](https://reuse.software/) convention:
license texts live once under `LICENSES/`, and every file states which
one applies to it, so nothing needs to be inferred from this file alone.

Files with no practical creative content (build-artifact reference
vectors, checksums, `.gitignore`) are left untagged.
`layers/meta-ast2600-secureboot/vbootrom-ast2600/test-vectors/` carries
its own separate `LICENSE-socsec.txt` for the vendored ASPEED `socsec`
reference material, unrelated to either license above.
